From: Deividas Nastajus <16858119+dns54@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/25] UefiPayloadPkg: Handle the boot watchdog at ReadyToBoot

coreboot can arm the Intel PCH TCO timer early in boot, so a hang before
the first boot attempt resets the system. Add TcoWatchdogDxe, which acts
on coreboot's "watchdog" setup option at each ReadyToBoot:
- Boot Only (1): halt the timer, as the OS loader takes over.
- Boot and OS (2): clear a first timeout and reload the timer, so the
  OS gets the full window to start its own watchdog driver.

Loading the setup app (UiApp) or the boot manager menu halts the timer
in either mode, so a user can take their time there. Launching the boot
manager menu doesn't signal ReadyToBoot. On a capsule update boot the
driver halts the timer right away, so a reset can't interrupt a flash
write.

It finds the timer through the SMBus controller's TCOBASE and does
nothing if the timer isn't running.

Signed-off-by: Deividas Nastajus <16858119+dns54@users.noreply.github.com>
